Parent: 1544

## Context

Addition 1 of `design/2026-11-12-guichet-inter-repo-dialogue.md` § 5: wake an owner at filing. In the trial (`design/research/2026-11-12-guichet-triage-trial.md`),
the one foreign ticket still untouched (G4) is the case this catches.

## Scope

- `rules/workflow.md` § Cross-project work: the asker logs
  `filed from <asker-repo> <asker-ticket>` on the ticket it files in the
  receiver's store (erg's header set is closed, so provenance goes in the
  log); when timing matters it also tells a live session, as today.
- `/molt` and `/dashboard` list open tickets carrying such a line that
  nobody has picked up (no branch or worktree lock naming the ticket) after
  a day.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The convention is stated once in `rules/workflow.md`; callers cite it.
- [ ] On a test store, a foreign ticket older than a day with no branch is
      listed by both skills and disappears once a branch names it.
- [ ] `make check` passes.
